{
  "id": "RAW_84e3f8fed2",
  "title": "NVIDIA 发布 CUDA Rust，推出 cuda-oxide（SIMT）与 cutile-rs（Tile）项目，实现编译期安全的 GPU 内核",
  "url": "https://www.marktechpost.com/2026/09/08/nvidia-announces-cuda-rust-with-cuda-oxide-simt-and-cutile-rs-tile-for-compile-time-safe-gpu-kernels/",
  "date": "2026-09-09 03:51:56",
  "author": "Asif Razzaq",
  "siteName": "MarkTechPost",
  "content": "<html>\n <head></head>\n <body>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">NVIDIA has <a href=\"https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/introducing-cuda-rust-two-tracks-for-writing-gpu-kernels/\">announced CUDA Rust</a>, a push to make Rust a first-class language for writing GPU kernels. Rust code could already launch CUDA kernels, but the kernel body usually had to be written elsewhere. CUDA Rust closes that gap with two NVlabs open-source projects: <a href=\"https://github.com/NVlabs/cuda-oxide\">cuda-oxide</a> for the SIMT model and <a href=\"https://github.com/NVlabs/cutile-rs\">cutile-rs</a> for the newer Tile model. Both compile Rust kernels natively and use Rust’s ownership rules to reject aliasing bugs at compile time.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Is it deployable?</strong> Partially. cutile-rs is <a href=\"https://crates.io/crates/cutile\">published on crates.io</a>, runs on stable Rust 1.89+, and is already used in Hugging Face’s <a href=\"https://github.com/huggingface/grout\">Grout</a> inference engine and in <a href=\"https://github.com/EricLBuehler/mistral.rs\">mistral.rs</a>. cuda-oxide is early alpha. The both projects are in alpha phase and not confirmed for production.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-why-rust-for-the-gpu-kernel\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Why Rust for the GPU Kernel</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The systems layer of AI, from inference engines to drivers and agent runtimes, is increasingly written in Rust. NVIDIA’s Nova Linux driver is in Rust, <a href=\"https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/ai/dynamo/\">NVIDIA Dynamo</a> has a Rust core, and NVTX has Rust bindings. The GPU kernel was the exception.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The two tracks mirror the two programming models CUDA already offers. <strong>SIMT</strong> is the model used in CUDA C++ and <a href=\"https://nvidia.github.io/numba-cuda/\">numba-cuda</a>: you describe what one thread does and launch thousands of them. <strong>Tile</strong> is the newer model, also available in <a href=\"https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/cuda-tile-cpp-api-reference/\">C++</a> and <a href=\"https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/cutile-python/\">Python</a>: you describe what one tile of data does, and the <a href=\"https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/tile-ir/latest/index.html\">Tile IR compiler</a> handles thread mapping and memory layout. NVIDIA recommends Tile first, with SIMT for explicit thread and memory control. Planned inter-language interop means choosing Rust will not lock developers out of C++ or Python.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-the-simt-track-cuda-oxide\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>The SIMT Track: cuda-oxide</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">cuda-oxide is a custom <code>rustc</code> codegen backend. It routes <code>#[kernel]</code> functions through Rust MIR, the community <a href=\"https://github.com/pliron-org/pliron\">Pliron</a> IR framework, and LLVM IR down to PTX, then hands everything else to the standard backend. NVIDIA wrote the GPU dialects on top of Pliron.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Requirements: Linux, a GPU with compute capability 8.0 or later, CUDA 12.x or newer, clang with libclang, and a pinned nightly toolchain (<code>nightly-2026-04-03</code>). <code>cargo oxide doctor</code> checks the setup and <code>cargo oxide new</code> scaffolds a vector addition program, with host and device code in one file.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The safety argument sits in the kernel signature. Inputs <code>a</code> and <code>b</code> are ordinary shared slices. The output <code>c</code> is a <code>DisjointSlice&lt;f32&gt;</code>, a type that gives each thread exclusive access to its own element. A plain <code>&amp;mut [f32]</code> would need every thread to hold the same mutable borrow, which Rust refuses. <code>c.get_mut(idx)</code> returns an <code>Option</code>, so out-of-bounds access becomes a handled branch. A <code>#[launch_contract]</code> attribute declares the block shape, and the generated <code>prepare_vecadd</code> method validates the launch configuration against it before the safe launch runs.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-the-tile-track-cutile-rs\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>The Tile Track: cutile-rs</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">cutile-rs works one level higher. Each tile block runs the kernel body once as a single logical thread over one sub-tensor, and the compiler decides how many real GPU threads back it. The <code>#[cutile::module]</code> macro embeds the kernel’s AST in the host binary and JIT-compiles it through CUDA Tile IR when the kernel is first launched.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Requirements are lighter: compute capability 8.0 or later, CUDA 13.3, stable Rust 1.89 or newer, and Linux, with no nightly and no custom LLVM. Setup is <code>cargo new</code>, then <code>cargo add cutile</code>.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The host-side <code>.partition([128])</code> call does 3 jobs. It gives each tile exclusive ownership of its 128-element chunk, fixes the grid at 1,024 / 128 = 8 tiles, and supplies the const tile width <code>B</code>. Input tensors use <code>-1</code> as a dynamic dimension resolved at launch. The generated launcher takes ownership of all tensors and returns them when the GPU finishes. Nothing executes until <code>.sync_on(&amp;stream)</code>; everything before it is a lazy description recorded in one chain.</p>\n  <div id=\"mtp-cuda-rust-explainer\" style=\"width:100%!important;margin:24px 0!important;\">\n   <iframe class=\"lazyload\" id=\"mtp-cuda-rust-frame\" title=\"CUDA Rust interactive explainer by Marktechpost\" scrolling=\"no\" srcdoc=\"&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta charset=&quot;utf-8&quot;&gt;&lt;meta name=&quot;viewport&quot; content=&quot;width=device-width,initial-scale=1&quot;&gt;\n&lt;style&gt;\n*{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0;padding:0}\nbody{background:#0a0a0a;background-image:radial-gradient(circle at 85% 0%,rgba(118,185,0,.22) 0%,rgba(118,185,0,0) 45%),linear-gradient(rgba(118,185,0,.06) 1px,transparent 1px),linear-gradient(90deg,rgba(118,185,0,.06) 1px,transparent 1px);background-size:auto,60px 60px,60px 60px;color:#e6e6e6;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;padding:18px}\n.wrap{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;border:1px solid #2c2c2c;border-radius:14px;background:rgba(14,14,14,.94);overflow:hidden}\n.hd{padding:16px 20px;border-bottom:1px solid #2a2a2a;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap}\n.hd .dot{width:10px;height:10px;border-radius:50%;background:#76B900;box-shadow:0 0 12px #76B900}\n.hd h2{font-size:17px;color:#fff;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:-.01em}\n.hd span{color:#8a8a8a;font-size:12px;margin-left:auto}\n.tabs{display:flex;border-bottom:1px solid #2a2a2a;overflow-x:auto}\n.tab{flex:1;min-width:140px;padding:12px 10px;background:none;border:none;color:#9a9a9a;font-size:13px;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;border-bottom:3px solid transparent;white-space:nowrap}\n.tab.on{color:#76B900;border-bottom-color:#76B900;background:#1a1f14}\n.panel{display:none;padding:20px}\n.panel.on{display:block}\n.lead{color:#bdbdbd;font-size:14px;line-height:1.55;margin-bottom:14px}\n.btn{background:#76B900;color:#0a0a0a;border:none;padding:9px 16px;border-radius:999px;font-weight:800;font-size:13px;cursor:pointer}\n.btn.alt{background:transparent;color:#76B900;border:2px solid #76B900}\n.btn:disabled{opacity:.5;cursor:default}\n.row{display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:14px}\n/* pipeline */\n.pipe{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px}\n.track{background:rgba(20,20,20,.88);border:1px solid #2c2c2c;border-left:6px solid #76B900;border-radius:12px;padding:14px}\n.track h3{font-size:15px;color:#76B900;font-weight:800;margin-bottom:10px}\n.stages{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px}\n.st{background:#222;border:1px solid #333;border-radius:6px;padding:8px 10px;font-size:12.5px;color:#9a9a9a;position:relative;transition:all .35s;transform:translateX(0)}\n.st b{color:#e6e6e6;display:block;font-size:13px}\n.st.lit{border-color:#76B900;background:#1f2a0f;color:#cfe5a3;box-shadow:0 0 10px rgba(118,185,0,.35)}\n.st.lit b{color:#fff}\n.arrow{text-align:center;color:#444;font-size:14px;line-height:1}\n.arrow.lit{color:#76B900}\n.note{font-size:12px;color:#8a8a8a;margin-top:10px;min-height:32px}\n/* threads vs tiles */\n.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(32,1fr);gap:2px;margin:10px 0}\n.cell{aspect-ratio:1;background:#262626;border-radius:2px;transition:background .25s,transform .25s}\n.cell.a{background:#76B900;transform:scale(1.15)}\n.cell.done{background:#3d5f00}\n.legend{display:flex;gap:16px;font-size:12px;color:#9a9a9a;flex-wrap:wrap}\n.legend i{display:inline-block;width:10px;height:10px;border-radius:2px;margin-right:5px;vertical-align:middle}\n.stat{font-family:Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:12.5px;color:#76B900;margin-top:8px;min-height:18px}\n/* aliasing */\n.code{background:#080808;border:1px solid #2a2a2a;border-radius:8px;padding:12px 14px;font-family:Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#d0d0d0;overflow-x:auto;white-space:pre}\n.code .k{color:#76B900}.code .t{color:#7cc7ff}.code .s{color:#ffb86c}\n.slot{display:inline-block;border:1px dashed #555;border-radius:4px;padding:0 6px;cursor:pointer;color:#ffb86c;transition:all .3s}\n.slot.bad{border-color:#ff5555;color:#ff5555;background:#2a1010}\n.slot.good{border-color:#76B900;color:#76B900}\n.err{margin-top:12px;padding:10px 12px;border-radius:6px;font-family:Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:1.5;opacity:0;transform:translateY(6px);transition:all .4s;min-height:60px}\n.err.show{opacity:1;transform:translateY(0)}\n.err.red{background:#160f0f;border:1px solid #6b2a2a;color:#ffb3b3}\n.err.green{background:#1f2a0f;border:1px solid #76B900;color:#cfe5a3}\n/* compare */\ntable{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13px}\nth,td{padding:9px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid #2a2a2a;text-align:left;vertical-align:top}\nth{color:#76B900;font-size:12px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.04em}\ntd:first-child{color:#9a9a9a;width:150px}\ntr.hi td{background:#1a2010}\n.pill{display:inline-block;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:999px;font-size:11px;font-weight:700}\n.pill.g{background:#76B900;color:#0a0a0a}.pill.y{background:#3a3a1a;color:#ffe066;border:1px solid #6b6b2a}\n.ft{padding:10px 20px;border-top:1px solid #2a2a2a;font-size:11.5px;color:#777;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px}\n.ft b{color:#76B900;letter-spacing:.06em}\n@media(max-width:640px){.pipe{grid-template-columns:1fr}.grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(16,1fr)}td:first-child{width:auto}body{padding:8px}}\n&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;&lt;body&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;wrap&quot; id=&quot;root&quot;&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;hd&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;dot&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;CUDA Rust Explainer: SIMT vs Tile&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;span&gt;Interactive. Click to explore.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;tabs&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button class=&quot;tab on&quot; data-p=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;1. Compile pipelines&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;button class=&quot;tab&quot; data-p=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;2. Threads vs tiles&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;button class=&quot;tab&quot; data-p=&quot;p3&quot;&gt;3. Aliasing check&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;button class=&quot;tab&quot; data-p=&quot;p4&quot;&gt;4. Requirements&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n\n&lt;div class=&quot;panel on&quot; id=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;\n&lt;p class=&quot;lead&quot;&gt;Both tracks turn Rust into GPU code, but they take different routes. cuda-oxide is an ahead-of-time rustc backend that emits PTX. cutile-rs captures the kernel AST and JIT-compiles it through CUDA Tile IR on first launch.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;&lt;button class=&quot;btn&quot; id=&quot;runPipe&quot;&gt;Animate both pipelines&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button class=&quot;btn alt&quot; id=&quot;resetPipe&quot;&gt;Reset&lt;/button&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;pipe&quot;&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;track&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;SIMT track: cuda-oxide&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;stages&quot; id=&quot;sA&quot;&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;st&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Rust source&lt;/b&gt;#[kernel] fn inside #[cuda_module]&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;arrow&quot;&gt;&amp;#9660;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;st&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Rust MIR&lt;/b&gt;custom rustc codegen backend intercepts&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;arrow&quot;&gt;&amp;#9660;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;st&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Pliron IR&lt;/b&gt;community IR framework with NVIDIA GPU dialects&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;arrow&quot;&gt;&amp;#9660;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;st&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;LLVM IR&lt;/b&gt;standard LLVM backend takes over&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;arrow&quot;&gt;&amp;#9660;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;st&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PTX&lt;/b&gt;embedded device bundle, launched via checked contract&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;note&quot; id=&quot;nA&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;track&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Tile track: cutile-rs&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;stages&quot; id=&quot;sB&quot;&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;st&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Rust source&lt;/b&gt;#[cutile::entry] fn inside #[cutile::module]&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;arrow&quot;&gt;&amp;#9660;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;st&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Captured AST&lt;/b&gt;proc macro embeds kernel AST in host binary&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;arrow&quot;&gt;&amp;#9660;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;st&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CUDA Tile IR&lt;/b&gt;JIT at first launch, compiler owns thread mapping&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;arrow&quot;&gt;&amp;#9660;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;st&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;GPU cubin&lt;/b&gt;per-specialization, keyed by tile width B&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;note&quot; id=&quot;nB&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n\n&lt;div class=&quot;panel&quot; id=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;\n&lt;p class=&quot;lead&quot;&gt;Same job: add 1,024 floats elementwise. SIMT launches 4 blocks of 256 threads and each thread owns 1 element. Tile partitions the output into 8 tiles of 128 and each tile block runs the body once as a single logical thread.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;&lt;button class=&quot;btn&quot; id=&quot;goSimt&quot;&gt;Run SIMT (4 x 256 threads)&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button class=&quot;btn&quot; id=&quot;goTile&quot;&gt;Run Tile (8 x 128 tiles)&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button class=&quot;btn alt&quot; id=&quot;resetGrid&quot;&gt;Reset&lt;/button&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;grid&quot; id=&quot;grid&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;legend&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;background:#262626&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;pending&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;background:#76B900&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;active&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;background:#3d5f00&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;written&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;stat&quot; id=&quot;stat&quot;&gt;1,024 elements, 32 per row&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n\n&lt;div class=&quot;panel&quot; id=&quot;p3&quot;&gt;\n&lt;p class=&quot;lead&quot;&gt;Rust's borrow checker rejects a kernel that reads and writes the same buffer. Click the highlighted argument to swap it and watch the compiler respond. This is the exact error class both tracks catch at compile time.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;&lt;button class=&quot;btn alt&quot; id=&quot;modeSimt&quot;&gt;cuda-oxide (SIMT)&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button class=&quot;btn alt&quot; id=&quot;modeTile&quot;&gt;cutile-rs (Tile)&lt;/button&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;code&quot; id=&quot;codeBox&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;err&quot; id=&quot;errBox&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n\n&lt;div class=&quot;panel&quot; id=&quot;p4&quot;&gt;\n&lt;p class=&quot;lead&quot;&gt;What you need to run each track today, per NVIDIA's announcement. Hover or tap a row to highlight it.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;table&gt;\n&lt;thead&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Requirement&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;cuda-oxide (SIMT)&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;cutile-rs (Tile)&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/thead&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Status&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;pill y&quot;&gt;Early alpha&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;pill g&quot;&gt;On crates.io&lt;/span&gt; used in Grout, mistral.rs&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Rust toolchain&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Pinned nightly-2026-04-03&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Stable 1.89 or newer&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;CUDA&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Toolkit 12.x or newer&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;CUDA 13.3&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;GPU&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Compute capability 8.0+&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Compute capability 8.0+&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;OS&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Linux&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Linux&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Extra deps&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;clang + libclang, optional system LLVM&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;None (no custom LLVM)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Install&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;cargo +nightly install cargo-oxide (git)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;cargo add cutile&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Compile&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Ahead of time to PTX&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;JIT via CUDA Tile IR&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Safety unit&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;DisjointSlice + launch contract per call&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Partitioned tensor ownership across launch&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Shared memory&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Available, requires unsafe today&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Managed by compiler&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n\n&lt;div class=&quot;ft&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Source: NVIDIA Technical Blog, Sept 8, 2026. Verified Sept 8, 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;MARKTECHPOST&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;script&gt;\n(function(){\nvar root=document.getElementById('root');\nfunction post(){try{parent.postMessage({type:'mtp-cuda-rust-h',h:root.offsetHeight+40},'*');}catch(e){}}\nwindow.addEventListener('load',post);window.addEventListener('resize',post);\n/* tabs */\nvar tabs=document.querySelectorAll('.tab');\ntabs.forEach(function(t){t.addEventListener('click',function(){\ntabs.forEach(function(x){x.classList.remove('on')});t.classList.add('on');\ndocument.querySelectorAll('.panel').forEach(function(p){p.classList.remove('on')});\ndocument.getElementById(t.getAttribute('data-p')).classList.add('on');post();});});\n/* pipeline */\nvar noteA=['Kernel functions are tagged for GPU compilation.','rustc hands #[kernel] MIR to the custom backend.','GPU dialects live here, written in Rust.','Transforms done; LLVM does the final lowering.','PTX is bundled and launched through prepare_vecadd().'];\nvar noteB=['Kernel body operates on tiles, not scalars.','No separate build step; the AST ships in your binary.','Compiler decides how many real threads back each tile.','Cached per B; a new tile width triggers a new build.'];\nvar timers=[];\nfunction clearT(){timers.forEach(clearTimeout);timers=[];}\nfunction resetPipe(){clearT();document.querySelectorAll('#sA .st,#sB .st,#sA .arrow,#sB .arrow').forEach(function(e){e.classList.remove('lit')});document.getElementById('nA').textContent='';document.getElementById('nB').textContent='';}\nfunction runTrack(id,noteId,notes){var kids=document.querySelectorAll('#'+id+' &gt; *');var i=0;kids.forEach(function(el,idx){timers.push(setTimeout(function(){el.classList.add('lit');if(el.classList.contains('st')){document.getElementById(noteId).textContent=notes[i++]||'';}post();},idx*420));});}\ndocument.getElementById('runPipe').onclick=function(){resetPipe();runTrack('sA','nA',noteA);runTrack('sB','nB',noteB);};\ndocument.getElementById('resetPipe').onclick=resetPipe;\n/* grid */\nvar grid=document.getElementById('grid');var cells=[];\nfor(var i=0;i&lt;1024;i++){var c=document.createElement('div');c.className='cell';grid.appendChild(c);cells.push(c);}\nvar gt=[];function gclear(){gt.forEach(clearTimeout);gt=[];}\nfunction resetGrid(){gclear();cells.forEach(function(c){c.className='cell'});document.getElementById('stat').textContent='1,024 elements, 32 per row';}\nfunction runSim(chunk,label,perStep){resetGrid();var n=1024/chunk;for(var b=0;b&lt;n;b++){(function(b){gt.push(setTimeout(function(){for(var j=b*chunk;j&lt;(b+1)*chunk;j++){cells[j].classList.add('a');}document.getElementById('stat').textContent=label(b);},b*perStep));gt.push(setTimeout(function(){for(var j=b*chunk;j&lt;(b+1)*chunk;j++){cells[j].classList.remove('a');cells[j].classList.add('done');}if(b===n-1){document.getElementById('stat').textContent='PASSED: all 1024 elements correct';}},b*perStep+perStep*0.8));})(b);}}\ndocument.getElementById('goSimt').onclick=function(){runSim(256,function(b){return 'block '+b+' of 4: 256 threads, thread::index_1d() = '+(b*256)+'..'+(b*256+255);},700);};\ndocument.getElementById('goTile').onclick=function(){runSim(128,function(b){return 'tile '+b+' of 8: one logical thread writes z['+(b*128)+'..'+(b*128+127)+']';},450);};\ndocument.getElementById('resetGrid').onclick=resetGrid;\n/* aliasing */\nvar mode='simt',bad=false;\nvar box=document.getElementById('codeBox'),err=document.getElementById('errBox');\nfunction render(){\nif(mode==='simt'){box.innerHTML='&lt;span class=&quot;k&quot;&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; a_dev = DeviceBuffer::from_host(&amp;amp;stream, &amp;amp;a_host)?;\\n&lt;span class=&quot;k&quot;&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; b_dev = DeviceBuffer::from_host(&amp;amp;stream, &amp;amp;b_host)?;\\n&lt;span class=&quot;k&quot;&gt;let mut&lt;/span&gt; c_dev = DeviceBuffer::&amp;lt;&lt;span class=&quot;t&quot;&gt;f32&lt;/span&gt;&amp;gt;::zeroed(&amp;amp;stream, N)?;\\n\\nmodule.vecadd(&amp;amp;stream, &amp;amp;prepared, &lt;span class=&quot;slot '+(bad?'bad':'good')+'&quot; id=&quot;slot&quot;&gt;'+(bad?'&amp;amp;c_dev':'&amp;amp;a_dev')+'&lt;/span&gt;, &amp;amp;b_dev, &amp;amp;&lt;span class=&quot;k&quot;&gt;mut&lt;/span&gt; c_dev)?;';\nerr.className='err show '+(bad?'red':'green');\nerr.innerHTML=bad?'error[E0502]: cannot borrow `c_dev` as mutable because it is also borrowed as immutable\\n\\nThe output DisjointSlice and an input slice point at the same buffer. Rejected before any GPU work runs.':'OK: a and b are shared borrows, c is the single mutable borrow.\\ncuda-oxide checks this at each launch call.';\n}else{box.innerHTML='&lt;span class=&quot;k&quot;&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; x = api::ones::&amp;lt;&lt;span class=&quot;t&quot;&gt;f32&lt;/span&gt;&amp;gt;(&amp;amp;[1024]);\\n&lt;span class=&quot;k&quot;&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; y = api::ones::&amp;lt;&lt;span class=&quot;t&quot;&gt;f32&lt;/span&gt;&amp;gt;(&amp;amp;[1024]);\\n&lt;span class=&quot;k&quot;&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; z = api::zeros::&amp;lt;&lt;span class=&quot;t&quot;&gt;f32&lt;/span&gt;&amp;gt;(&amp;amp;[1024]);\\n\\nkernel::add(z.partition([128]), &lt;span class=&quot;slot '+(bad?'bad':'good')+'&quot; id=&quot;slot&quot;&gt;'+(bad?'z':'x')+'&lt;/span&gt;, y)';\nerr.className='err show '+(bad?'red':'green');\nerr.innerHTML=bad?'error[E0382]: use of moved value: `z`\\n\\nThe launcher took ownership of z when it was partitioned. Ownership follows the tensor across the launch boundary.':'OK: z is partitioned into 8 exclusive tiles; x and y are shared.\\nNothing runs until .sync_on(&amp;amp;stream).';}\nerr.style.whiteSpace='pre-wrap';\ndocument.getElementById('slot').onclick=function(){bad=!bad;render();};\npost();}\ndocument.getElementById('modeSimt').onclick=function(){mode='simt';bad=false;render();};\ndocument.getElementById('modeTile').onclick=function(){mode='tile';bad=false;render();};\nrender();\n/* table hover */\ndocument.querySelectorAll('#p4 tbody tr').forEach(function(r){r.addEventListener('mouseenter',function(){r.classList.add('hi')});r.addEventListener('mouseleave',function(){r.classList.remove('hi')});r.addEventListener('click',function(){r.classList.toggle('hi')});});\nsetTimeout(post,300);\n})();\n&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;\n\"></iframe>\n  </div>\n  <h2 id=\"h-what-the-compiler-catches\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>What the Compiler Catches</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Passing the SIMT kernel’s output buffer as one of its own inputs fails with <code>error[E0502]: cannot borrow c_dev as mutable because it is also borrowed as immutable</code>. The same aliasing on the Tile side fails with <code>error[E0382]: use of moved value: z</code>. cuda-oxide checks each launch call; cutile-rs’s ownership follows tensors across the launch boundary, which NVIDIA calls the stronger guarantee.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Tile exposes no shared memory or thread indexing to misuse. SIMT keeps that control, but shared memory in cuda-oxide currently requires <code>unsafe</code>.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-key-takeaways\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Key Takeaways</strong></h2>\n  <ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n   <li>CUDA Rust adds 2 native GPU kernel tracks in Rust: cuda-oxide (SIMT) and cutile-rs (Tile).</li>\n   <li>cuda-oxide compiles Rust MIR through Pliron and LLVM to PTX; it needs a pinned nightly.</li>\n   <li>cutile-rs runs on stable Rust 1.89+ with CUDA 13.3 and JIT-compiles via CUDA Tile IR.</li>\n   <li>Both reject buffer aliasing at compile time using Rust’s borrow checker and ownership.</li>\n   <li>cutile-rs already powers Grout and mistral.rs; neither project is production-ready yet.</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>\n  <hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\">\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Check out the&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/introducing-cuda-rust-two-tracks-for-writing-gpu-kernels?\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Technical details here</a></strong>. Also,&nbsp;feel free to follow us on&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://x.com/intent/follow?screen_name=marktechpost\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><mark>Twitter</mark></a></strong>&nbsp;and don’t forget to join our&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/machinelearningnews/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">150k+ML SubReddit</a></strong>&nbsp;and Subscribe to&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://magic.beehiiv.com/v1/f5e63dd4-5653-4f09-83e2-321a8b1ba526?email={{email}}\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">our Newsletter</a></strong>. Wait! are you on telegram?&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://t.me/machinelearningresearchnews\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">now you can join us on telegram as well.</a></strong></p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Need to partner with us for promoting your GitHub Repo OR Hugging Face Page OR Product Release OR Webinar etc.?&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://forms.gle/wbash1wF6efRj8G58\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><mark>Connect with us</mark></a></strong></p>\n  <!-- MOLONGUI AUTHORSHIP PLUGIN 5.2.11 -->\n  <!-- https://www.molongui.com/wordpress-plugin-post-authors -->\n  <div class=\"m-a-box \" data-box-layout=\"slim\" data-box-position=\"below\" data-multiauthor=\"false\" data-author-id=\"1\" data-author-type=\"user\" data-author-archived=\"\">\n   <div class=\"m-a-box-container\">\n    <div class=\"m-a-box-tab m-a-box-content m-a-box-profile\" data-profile-layout=\"layout-1\" data-author-ref=\"user-1\" itemscope itemid=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/author/6flvq/\" itemtype=\"https://schema.org/Person\">\n     <div class=\"m-a-box-content-middle\">\n      <div class=\"m-a-box-item m-a-box-avatar\" data-source=\"local\">\n       <a class=\"m-a-box-avatar-url\" href=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/author/6flvq/\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM-150x150.png\" class=\"avatar avatar-150 photo\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM-150x150.png 150w, https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM-80x80.png 80w, https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM-24x24.png 24w, https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM-48x48.png 48w, https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM-96x96.png 96w, https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM-300x300.png 300w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px\" data-attachment-id=\"17663\" data-permalink=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/?attachment_id=17663\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM.png\" data-orig-size=\"832,778\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"Screen Shot 2021-09-14 at 9.02.24 AM\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM.png\"></a>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"m-a-box-item m-a-box-social \">\n       <div class=\"m-a-box-social-icon m-a-list-social-icon\">\n        <a class=\"m-icon-container m-ico-facebook m-ico-\" href=\"https://www.facebook.com/MarkTechPost/\" target=\"_self\" itemprop=\"sameAs\" aria-label=\"View Asif Razzaq's Facebook profile\"><i class=\"m-a-icon-facebook\"></i></a>\n       </div>\n       <div class=\"m-a-box-social-icon m-a-list-social-icon\">\n        <a class=\"m-icon-container m-ico-twitter m-ico-\" href=\"https://twitter.com/asifrazzaq1988\" target=\"_self\" itemprop=\"sameAs\" aria-label=\"View Asif Razzaq's Twitter profile\"><i class=\"m-a-icon-twitter\"></i></a>\n       </div>\n       <div class=\"m-a-box-social-icon m-a-list-social-icon\">\n        <a class=\"m-icon-container m-ico-linkedin m-ico-\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/asifrazzaq/\" target=\"_self\" itemprop=\"sameAs\" aria-label=\"View Asif Razzaq's Linkedin profile\"><i class=\"m-a-icon-linkedin\"></i></a>\n       </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"m-a-box-item m-a-box-data\">\n       <div class=\"m-a-box-name\">\n        <h5 itemprop=\"name\"><a class=\"m-a-box-name-url \" href=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/author/6flvq/\" itemprop=\"url\"> Asif Razzaq</a></h5>\n       </div>\n       <div class=\"m-a-box-item m-a-box-meta\">\n        <a href=\"https://www.marktechpost.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"m-a-box-string-web\">Website</span></a>&nbsp;<span class=\"m-a-box-meta-divider\">|</span>&nbsp; <a href=\"#\" class=\"m-a-box-data-toggle\" rel=\"nofollow\"><span class=\"m-a-box-string-more-posts\">+ posts</span></a>\n       </div>\n       <div class=\"m-a-box-bio\" itemprop=\"description\">\n        <p>Asif Razzaq is the CEO of Marktechpost Media Inc.. As a visionary entrepreneur and engineer, Asif is committed to harnessing the potential of Artificial Intelligence for social good. His most recent endeavor is the launch of an Artificial Intelligence Media Platform, Marktechpost, which stands out for its in-depth coverage of machine learning and deep learning news that is both technically sound and easily understandable by a wide audience. The platform boasts of over 2 million monthly views, illustrating its popularity among audiences.</p>\n       </div>\n       <div class=\"m-a-box-related\" data-related-layout=\"layout-1\"></div>\n      </div>\n     </div>\n    </div>\n   </div>\n  </div>\n  <!-- CONTENT END 2 -->\n </body>\n</html>",
  "aiSummary": "NVIDIA 发布了 CUDA Rust，包含两个 NVlabs 项目：面向 SIMT 的 cuda-oxide 与面向 Tile 的 cutile-rs，借助所有权与借用检查机制，在 Rust 中实现编译期安全的 GPU 内核。",
  "oneSentenceSummary": "NVIDIA 发布了 CUDA Rust，包含两个 NVlabs 项目：面向 SIMT 的 cuda-oxide 与面向 Tile 的 cutile-rs，借助所有权与借用检查机制，在 Rust 中实现编译期安全的 GPU 内核。",
  "summary": "NVIDIA 推出了 CUDA Rust，这是一个让 Rust 成为 GPU 内核开发一流语言的框架。它包含两个开源项目：面向 SIMT 模型的 cuda-oxide 与面向 Tile 模型的 cutile-rs。cuda-oxide 采用自定义 rustc 代码生成后端，将内核函数经 Rust MIR、Pliron 与 LLVM 路由至 PTX，需要固定版本的 nightly 工具链。cutile-rs 在更高层级运行，嵌入内核 AST 并通过 CUDA Tile IR 进行 JIT 编译，可在 Rust 1.89+ 稳定版与 CUDA 13.3 上运行。两个项目均利用 Rust 的所有权与借用检查机制在编译期拒绝缓冲区别名问题，其中 cutile-rs 通过跨启动边界跟踪所有权提供了更强的保证。cutile-rs 已被 Hugging Face 的 Grout 与 mistral.rs 使用，但两个项目均处于 alpha 阶段，尚未达到生产就绪状态。",
  "mainPoints": [
    {
      "point": "CUDA Rust 在 Rust 中引入了两条原生 GPU 内核路径：cuda-oxide 面向 SIMT，cutile-rs 面向 Tile。",
      "explanation": "这填补了 Rust 此前只能启动 CUDA 内核、但内核主体需用其他语言编写的空白。两条路径与现有 CUDA 编程模型对应，开发者可在显式线程控制与更高层级的 Tile 抽象之间做出选择。"
    },
    {
      "point": "借助 Rust 的所有权与借用检查机制，在编译期拒绝缓冲区别名问题。",
      "explanation": "cuda-oxide 使用 DisjointSlice 等类型为每个线程提供独占访问权，而 cutile-rs 则跨启动边界跟踪张量所有权。这能在运行时之前预防数据竞争与越界访问等常见 GPU 缺陷。"
    },
    {
      "point": "cutile-rs 比 cuda-oxide 更易于部署。",
      "explanation": "cutile-rs 可在 Rust 1.89+ 稳定版与 CUDA 13.3 上运行，并已发布至 crates.io，且已被 Hugging Face 的 Grout 与 mistral.rs 采用。cuda-oxide 仍处于早期 alpha 阶段，需要固定版本的 nightly 工具链与自定义 LLVM，生产就绪度较低。"
    },
    {
      "point": "两个项目均处于 alpha 阶段，尚未确认可用于生产环境。",
      "explanation": "尽管 cutile-rs 已在真实项目中使用，但 NVIDIA 尚未确认任一项目可用于生产。开发者在关键系统中采用前，应评估其稳定性与支持情况。"
    }
  ],
  "keyQuotes": [
    "两者均原生编译 Rust 内核，并利用 Rust 的所有权规则在编译期拒绝别名缺陷。",
    "生成的启动器接管所有张量的所有权，并在 GPU 完成后将其返回。",
    "cuda-oxide 检查每次启动调用；cutile-rs 的所有权则跨启动边界跟踪张量，NVIDIA 称其为更强的保证。"
  ],
